// PROVENANCE EXTENSION - Origin and Extraction Information
//
// This extension tracks the source of statechart elements for:
//    - Extracted statecharts (from source code, binaries, documentation)
//    - Generated statecharts (from specifications, models, AI)
//    - Imported statecharts (format conversions from SCXML, XState, etc.)
//
// DESIGN RATIONALE:
// When statecharts are extracted from existing systems, provenance enables:
//    - Debugging: trace back to original source location
//    - Re-extraction: detect drift from source
//    - Auditing: compliance, security, license tracking
//    - Attribution: copyright, authorship, tool chains
//    - Verification: confidence scores, review status
//
// This extension follows the W3C PROV-O ontology concepts while providing
// a practical schema for statechart-specific needs.
//
// USE CASES:
// 1. Zelda3 extractor: ROM address → state/transition mapping
// 2. Source code analysis: function/line → guard expression
// 3. SCXML import: preserve original element IDs
// 4. AI generation: track model, prompt, confidence
// 5. Regulatory compliance: audit trail for safety-critical systems
// 6. License tracking: SPDX compliance for extracted code
//
// REFERENCES:
// \[PROV-O\] W3C PROV-O: The PROV Ontology, <https://www.w3.org/TR/prov-o/>
// \[SPDX\] Software Package Data Exchange, <https://spdx.dev/>
// \[CycloneDX\] OWASP CycloneDX SBOM Standard
