// ===========================================================================
// TESTING EXTENSION - Test Scenarios and Coverage
//
// This extension provides test case definitions, expected execution traces,
// and coverage tracking for statechart testing tools.
//
// DESIGN RATIONALE:
// Testing statecharts requires:
//    1. Defining event sequences (inputs)
//    2. Specifying expected configurations (outputs)
//    3. Tracking state/transition coverage
//    4. Supporting property-based invariants
//
// This extension standardizes these concerns for interoperability between
// test runners, coverage tools, and model checkers.
//
// TESTING APPROACHES SUPPORTED:
// 1. Trace-based testing: specific event sequences with expected outcomes
// 2. Property-based testing: invariants that must hold in any execution
// 3. Coverage-based testing: ensure all states/transitions are exercised
// 4. Mutation testing: verify tests detect injected faults
//
// USE CASES:
// 1. Automated test execution with sc CLI
// 2. CI/CD integration for statechart validation
// 3. Coverage reporting and gap analysis
// 4. Regression test suites
// 5. Property-based test generation
// 6. Mutation testing frameworks
//
// REFERENCES:
// \[UTP2\] UML Testing Profile 2.0, OMG
// \[MBT\] Model-Based Testing, Utting & Legeard
// \[QuickCheck\] Property-Based Testing, Claessen & Hughes
// ===========================================================================

// ─────────────────────────── Test Suite ────────────────────────────────────

/// *
/// TestSuite groups related test cases.
///
/// STORAGE:
/// Can be attached to Statechart-level extensions or stored separately.
///
/// EXECUTION SEMANTICS:
/// 1. Run setup actions before each test
